# Claim: a build cut short midway, past its step limit, ended by the system
# as memory runs out (the SIGKILL the kernel sends its compile-time
# process), or cancelled, publishes nothing of what it generated and records
# no fact: the modules and the program of the last good build stay byte for
# byte and no staged file is left. The stop is reported, ahead of the staged
# report on the name the build never made. The next run starts clean: it
# builds the same modules and the same program as before the stops.
# stalls.txt changes `first`, then loops before it generates `second`, so the
# stop comes between the two generations and `second` is never promised: its
# name is an ordinary unknown name; comptime.sh finds the process `build: fn`
# runs in.
requires: os:unix
requires: tool:sh
requires: tool:pgrep
fixture: Fixtures/GenerateCancelMidway
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
step good: jet build main.jet
exit: 0
copy: .jet/generated/main/first.jet good.first
copy: .jet/generated/main/second.jet good.second
copy: .jet/build/app good.app
step launch: {work}/.jet/build/app
exit: 0
stdout: = "42\n"
copy: stalls.txt main.jet
step steps: jet build main.jet
exit: 1
stderr: ~ "Jet.ComptimeFuelExhausted" # the step limit stops the build midway, and is reported
stderr: ~ "Nothing named `second_value` exists here" # then the staged report on the name it never made
file: .jet/generated/main/first.jet == good.first # the changed `first` was never published
file: .jet/generated/main/second.jet == good.second
file: .jet/generated/main/first.jet.writing absent
file: .jet/build/app == good.app # nothing was compiled or linked
spawn memory: jet build main.jet
stderr: file memory.stderr
step: sh comptime.sh {pid:memory} KILL
exit: 0
stdout: = "running\n" # `build: fn` was running when its process was killed
wait: memory timeout 60s
exit: nonzero
file: memory.stderr ~ "Jet.ComptimeEndedBySignal" # the kill is reported
file: memory.stderr ~ "ended by SIGKILL from outside jet" # the signal and who sent it
file: memory.stderr ~ "Nothing named `second_value` exists here" # the staged report the stop left
file: .jet/generated/main/first.jet == good.first
file: .jet/generated/main/second.jet == good.second
file: .jet/generated/main/first.jet.writing absent
file: .jet/build/app == good.app
spawn cancel: jet build main.jet
stderr: file cancel.stderr
step: sh comptime.sh {pid:cancel}
exit: 0
stdout: = "running\n" # `build: fn` is running
signal cancel: INT
wait: cancel timeout 60s
exit: nonzero # the cancel ends the build
file: .jet/generated/main/first.jet == good.first
file: .jet/generated/main/second.jet == good.second
file: .jet/generated/main/first.jet.writing absent
file: .jet/build/app == good.app
copy: good.txt main.jet
step again: jet build main.jet
exit: 0
file: .jet/generated/main/first.jet == good.first # the next run starts clean
file: .jet/generated/main/second.jet == good.second
file: .jet/build/app == good.app
step relaunch: {work}/.jet/build/app
exit: 0
stdout: = "42\n"
